## 5. Current booking flow

1. Load preferred businesses for normal users; load all businesses for `ROLE_BUSINESS`.
2. Select business.
3. Fetch all business services; client filters `active === true`.
4. Fetch disabled dates.
5. Select service by service name; derive duration client-side.
6. Select date using Flatpickr, constrained to today through three months ahead.
7. Fetch slots using date, duration, and business ID.
8. Select available start time; calculate end time client-side.
9. Optionally enter `remark`.
10. Submit `POST /api/reservations`.
11. Show toast and navigate to `/`.

No review state, success screen, submit-pending state, loading state, recovery UI, or explicit stale-slot treatment exists.

## 6. Current personal reservation flow

1. Load paged reservation query.
2. Load reserved businesses for filter options.
3. Load services when a business filter is selected.
4. Filter by date range, business, service, status, and keyword.
5. Sort and paginate.
6. Render desktop table or mobile cards.
7. Cancel:
   - `PENDING`: immediate POST without a confirmation dialog.
   - `CONFIRMED`: Bootstrap modal requests a cancellation reason.
8. Reload the list after mutation.

There is no dedicated upcoming/history organization, reservation detail, rebook, edit, or reschedule.

## 7. Backend booking contracts

| Operation | Contract | Auth | Authoritative behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| Business list | `GET /api/businesses` → `{ success, message, data: BusinessResponse[] }` | Required | Returns `id`, `name`, `category`, `phone`, `address`, `slotInterval` |
| Preferred businesses | `GET /api/preferred-businesses` → same business list shape | Required | Customer preference list, not public discovery |
| Services | `GET /api/businesses/{businessId}/services` → `ServiceItemResponse[]` | Required | `id`, `name`, `duration`, `active` |
| Disabled dates | `GET /api/reservations/disabled-dates?businessId=` → `string[]` | Required | Closed overrides plus weekly closed days through server date + 3 months |
| Slots | `GET /api/reservations/slots?date=YYYY-MM-DD&duration=n&businessId=` → `{ time, available }[]` | Required | Availability snapshot, not held inventory |
| Create reservation | `POST /api/reservations` body `{ businessId, reservationDate, startTime, endTime, title, description?, remark? }` | Required | Ignores client `endTime` for persistence; resolves service by business ID + title, recalculates end time, locks business row, validates availability, creates `PENDING` reservation |

Create returns `201` with `ReservationResponse`. Invalid arguments return `400`; unavailable/invalid state returns `409`; unauthenticated requests return `401`; unexpected errors return `500`.

## 8. Backend reservation-management contracts

| Operation | Contract | Auth | Behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| Query own reservations | `POST /api/reservations/customer/query?page&size&sortBy&sortDir` | Required | Body: `startDate`, `endDate`, `service`, `status`, `businessId`, `keyword`; server scopes to current user |
| Reserved-business filter list | `GET /api/reservations/customer/reserved-businesses` | Required | Distinct businesses from the current customer’s reservation history |
| Cancel | `POST /api/reservations/{id}/cancel` body optional `{ cancelReason }` | Required | Server fetches by reservation ID and current user; ownership is backend-authoritative |
| Customer reservation detail | Unavailable in current backend | — | Query response is the only customer reservation representation |
| Reschedule | Unavailable in current backend | — | No endpoint or service behavior |
| Update booking/customer details | Unavailable in current backend | — | No endpoint |
| Rebook/duplicate | Unavailable in current backend | — | No endpoint |

`ReservationResponse` exposes `id`, `userId`, `username`, `businessId`, `businessName`, date/time, status, title, description, remark, cancelReason, createdAt, and updatedAt. Family 2 must normalize and selectively display it; it must not surface internal IDs.

## 9. Reservation status/state machine

| Backend state | Customer meaning | Customer action | Merchant action | Terminal | Family 2 grouping |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `PENDING` | Booking submitted; business has not confirmed | Cancel immediately | Confirm or cancel | No | Upcoming if end time is future |
| `CONFIRMED` | Booking confirmed | Request cancellation with required reason | Cancel | No | Upcoming if end time is future |
| `CANCEL_REQUESTED` | Customer cancellation awaits business decision | No repeat cancel | Approve → `CANCELLED`; reject → `CONFIRMED` | No | Operational/pending, not normal upcoming |
| `CANCELLED` | Booking cancelled | None | None | Yes | History |
| `COMPLETED` | Reservation end time has passed; scheduler or mutation path marks complete | None | None | Yes | History |

Automatic completion runs every five minutes for `PENDING`, `CONFIRMED`, and `CANCEL_REQUESTED` reservations after `reservationDate + endTime`.

## 10. Booking state machine

```text
Business source loading
  → business selected
  → services + disabled dates loading
  → active service selected
  → date selected
  → availability loading
  → available slot selected
  → optional remark entered
  → submit
  → backend revalidation
      → 201: reservation created as PENDING
      → 400: retain draft, associate error with field
      → 409: retain business/service/date/remark; clear slot; refresh slots
      → 401: auth handoff with safe returnTo
      → 500: retain full draft and provide retry
```

Changing business invalidates service, date, slot, and end time. Changing service invalidates slot and end time. Changing date invalidates slot and end time. Availability must be rechecked immediately before submit through the existing create mutation; no slot is reserved before successful creation.

## 11. Availability/concurrency behavior

- Slots are generated server-side from date-specific hours or weekly default hours.
- Slot interval comes from `BusinessData.slotInterval`, defaulting to 30 minutes.
- A slot is unavailable if it is in the past today or overlaps any non-`CANCELLED` reservation.
- `CANCEL_REQUESTED` still blocks availability.
- Disabled dates cover closed dates and closed weekly days, for the server’s today-to-three-month range.
- Create obtains a business database lock, reloads the service, recalculates slot availability, and rejects unavailable slots with `409` / `該時段已被預約`.
- There is no hold, reservation lease, timer, or client-side guarantee.
- Date and time use Java `LocalDate` / `LocalTime`; no business timezone is stored or returned.
- Frontend uses `new Date()` and Flatpickr local browser time, while backend uses server-local time. This is an unresolved timezone consistency risk.

## 12. Authentication/role boundary

- Anonymous users cannot enter either Family 2 route; `RequireAuth` redirects to `/login?returnTo=<encoded pathname+search>`.
- Login sanitizes return destinations through its internal return-to helper and uses session storage.
- Session-expired API requests emit the session-expired event and lead to login; current booking draft is not persisted.
- `PasswordResetGuard` redirects `mustChangePassword` users to `/force-change-password`.
- `BusinessSetupGuard` redirects incomplete business accounts to `/business/setup`.
- `/reservation/new` lacks a customer-role guard: a business user can navigate directly and receives all businesses; the backend creates a reservation for the authenticated business user. This is a role-boundary defect to resolve before redesign implementation.
- `/my/reservations` redirects business users only after render/effect; it is not guarded structurally.
- LINE login/account-link is outside Family 2 except as an existing authenticated-session source.

