## 39. Domain/normalization architecture

Define frontend models separate from raw DTOs:

- `BusinessBookingContext`: `id`, `name`, `category`, `phone`, `address`, `slotInterval`
- `BookingService`: `id`, `name`, `duration`, `active`
- `AvailabilityDate`: ISO local date string
- `TimeSlot`: `time`, `available`
- `BookingDraft`: business ID, service ID/name, duration, date, start time, derived end time, remark
- `BookingConfirmation`: normalized creation response
- `ReservationSummary`: safe list fields only
- `ReservationStatus`: exact backend enum plus semantic category
- `CancellationCapability`: derived only from status, reservation end time, and current backend rules

Valid helpers:

- `canCancelReservation(reservation, now)`
- `requiresCancellationReason(status)`
- `isUpcomingReservation(reservation, now)`
- `isHistoryReservation(reservation, now)`

Do not add generic policy, reschedule, staff, pricing, or reference helpers.

## 40. Cache/refresh architecture

No global query client exists.

- Keep route-local request state.
- Reload booking business context explicitly after retry.
- Reload services and disabled dates when business changes.
- Reload slots when business/service/date changes and after `409`.
- Refresh customer list after cancellation.
- Preserve prior list data if a refresh fails after initial success; mark it stale.
- No AuthContext refresh is required after booking/cancellation; these mutations do not change auth identity.
- Session expiry remains owned by the existing shared request/session event behavior.

## 41. Timezone/date contract

- Business timezone: unavailable in current model/API.
- Backend scheduling: server-local `LocalDate`, `LocalTime`, and `LocalDateTime`.
- Frontend: browser-local `Date`, Flatpickr `Y-m-d`, and raw time-string display.
- Reservation responses carry local date/time values without offset.
- Family 2 must present dates/times as “店家時間” only after a backend business-timezone decision; it must not silently convert values to user-local time.
- DST behavior is undefined because no zone is persisted.
- Preserve ISO local date strings without `new Date("YYYY-MM-DD")` conversion, which can shift dates by browser timezone.

## 42. Accessibility contract

- One `h1` per Family 2 route.
- Logical heading order.
- Label every input and associate all errors with controls.
- Use accessible step/progress semantics.
- Date picker requires keyboard support and visible focus.
- Slot controls require names including time and availability; selected state cannot rely only on color.
- Disabled slots require a textual reason.
- Mutation results require polite/assertive live-region feedback as appropriate.
- Dialog/bottom sheet requires title, description, focus trap, background inertness, close behavior, and focus restoration.
- Minimum 44px mobile targets.
- Visible focus and reduced-motion support.
- Status must use icon plus text.
- Destructive actions must explicitly say “取消預約” or “送出取消申請.”

## 43. Security/privacy contract

- Do not render raw reservation IDs, user IDs, or business IDs.
- Do not expose `username`, internal customer identity, or internal exception text beyond user-safe messages.
- Show customer remark only to the authenticated owner; backend ownership remains authoritative.
- Preserve cookie credentials and CSRF token behavior for mutations.
- Preserve `returnTo` internal-path sanitization; do not create open redirects.
- Do not log booking drafts, remarks, session tokens, or CSRF tokens.
- Frontend capability controls supplement—not replace—backend ownership/state enforcement.
- Do not display `description`, `cancelReason`, or any customer note outside the authorized owner context.

